`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`
**Build System Caching as Mental Model for LLM Prompt Efficiency:**
1. Anthropic's prompt cache is structurally identical to a remote build cache — it keys on prefix content hash. Any non-deterministic input (timestamps, session IDs, random paths) defeats it.
2. The flux-drive pipeline injects timestamps at multiple levels: OUTPUT_DIR, REVIEW_FILE path, findings timestamps. This is analogous to embedding `$(date)` in Bazel action inputs — no action is hermetic, so no cache hits.
3. Content-addressed paths (`sha256(content)[:12]` instead of `date +%s`) would make most prompts cache-friendly without changing semantics.
`─────────────────────────────────────────────────`

